 "text": "Hey there, how are you doing? That's one of the habits, 'work from wherever you want each week.' Set a day each week as your cutoff time, and in theory, you stop then. That's okay, I'll wait. Another helpful rule is 'no work after dinner.' Many people find a weekend off if they finish all their Monday tasks. 'No Work After Dinner rule, have Monday cut off time and a weekend off rule, and see how it feels. There' no harm in trying. I think you found the one that works for you. Change up every few months too, tired the rule.",
